Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Get emergency medical help if you have signs of an allergic reaction to albuterol: hives; difficult breathing; swelling of your face, lips, tongue, or throat.
Call your doctor at once if you have:
- wheezing, choking, or other breathing problems after using this medicine;
- chest pain, fast heart rate, pounding heartbeats or fluttering in your chest;
- pain or burning when you urinate;
- increased thirst, increased urination, hunger, dry mouth, fruity breath odor, drowsiness, dry skin, blurred vision, weight loss; or
- signs of low potassium - leg cramps, constipation, irregular heartbeats, fluttering in your chest, extreme thirst, increased urination, numbness or tingling, muscle weakness or limp feeling.
Common albuterol side effects may include:
- chest pain, fast or pounding heartbeats;
- upset stomach, vomiting;
- painful urination;
- dizziness;
- feeling shaky or nervous;
- headache, back pain, body aches; or
- cough, sore throat, sinus pain, runny or stuffy nose.
Triplet: ["Albuterol Inhalation", "has sign of low potassium", "irregular heartbeats"]

The relation 'has sign of low potassium' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug may lead to or be associated with the clinical sign specified by the object entity, indicating a potential low potassium level.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'lowers level of': The subject drug decreases the level of the substance or biomarker specified by the object entity in the body.
B. 'has test interference effect': The subject drug may cause a false positive or false negative result in the specified diagnostic test.
C. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
D. 'requires monitoring of': Patients taking the subject drug may need the medical test or monitoring specified by the object entity.
E. 'increases risk of': Taking the subject drug may raise the patient's likelihood of experiencing the condition or event specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
